Execute rules assigned at the site root when the site root itself is modified.

A rule assigned to the site root never ran for an edit to the site root: the
``modified`` handler returns unless the object is ``IContentish`` (``PloneSite``
is not), and ``execute_rules`` dispatches on ``aq_parent``, which for the site
root is the Zope application root and is not rule-assignable. The control panel
reported such a rule as active, so there was no sign anything had been skipped.

This matters on a Plone 6 / Volto site, where the homepage's blocks live on the
site root and ``plone.restapi`` notifies ``ObjectModifiedEvent`` on it: the most
frequently edited page was the one page no rule ever ran for.
